\section{discFA as a New R Package}\label{sec:discFA}

In this section, we describe \texttt{discFA} package with eight different models for various count data models. We start with the Poisson and negative binomial distributions. We then add the truncated and zero-inflated models to create more flexibly for various data analysis.  Table \ref{table1} summarizes all the eight functions developed for this package. As it is clear from Table \ref{table1}, the syntax for the \texttt{discFA} is quite easy to use. Also for each model, the AIC of the best model (lowest AIC), estimated models and factor parameters are displayed. 
