\section{Limitation of the discFA Package}\label{sec:limit}

The \texttt{discFA} package can run the factor analysis for many discrete data sets. There is no specific issue except highly negatively correlated variables (less than -0.50). For instance, there was a high negative correlation  ($-0.58$) between two variables in the last example ($x_3,x_4$) which turned out to have an independent model given below (with the warning message):
\begin{lstlisting}[language=R]
