$$R(z)=1+z+\frac{z^{2}}{2}+\frac{z^{3}}{6}+\frac{z^{4}}{24}+\frac{z^{5}}{120}-\frac{37z^{6}}{21600}-\frac{z^{7}}{540}-\frac{7z^{8}}{27000}-\frac{z^{9}}{6750}-\frac{z^{10}}{27000}. $$
\end{description}
Clearly, for both cases, we have
\begin{eqnarray*}
\mathcal{R}(z)-e^z=\mathcal{O}(z^6),
\end{eqnarray*}
thus verifying the fifth-order accuracy of the scheme.

