\begin{definition}
    \label{def: rank}
    We denote by {\BF $\Lambda_F^\star(p)$} the largest of the $\Lambda_F^\alpha(p)$.
    We say $F$ is a {\BF flow of rank $\alpha$} if $\alpha$ is the smallest ordinal such that $\Lambda_F^\star(p)=\Lambda_F^\alpha(p)$ for every $p\in X$. 
    Analogously, we denote by {\BF $D^\star_F(p)$} the set $\cO_F^+(p)\cup\Lambda_F^\star(p)$.
