By Corollary~\ref{cor: open orbits}, each orbit of a regular flow is unbounded for $t\to\pm\infty$.
Hence, each regular flow determines a family of continuous open curves that go to infinity at both ends and whose union is the whole plane.
\begin{definition}
    \label{def: fol}
    By {\bf foliation of the plane} we mean a family of continuous planar curves with the following properties:
