In the following examples we evaluate $\Lambda^\star$ and rank (see Definition~\ref{def: rank}) of several smooth wandering flows.
Throughout the examples, will denote by $\fL_\xi H$ the directional (Lie) derivative of the function $H$ along the vector field $\xi$, namely 
$$
\fL_\xi H(p) = {d\over dt}\bigg|_{t=0}(H\circ F^t_\xi)(p),
%\lim_{t\to0}{H(F^t_\xi(p))-H(p)\over t},
$$
where $F^t_\xi$ is the (local) flow of $\xi$.
Notice that, if $K\in C^1(X)$ is a strict Lyapunov function for the flow of a continuous vector field $\xi$, then $\fL_\xi K>0$ at every point.

