This case enjoys the following particularly strong and crucial property: 
%e following is a key property of wandering flows on the Euclidean plane:
%(in Lemma~\ref{lemma: prec}), besides the results of Haefliger and Reeb and the second author, is that each orbit $\gamma$ of a wandering flow $F$ on $\bR^2$ divides the plane into two disjoint path-connected open sets. 
