\begin{definition}
    Given a binary relation $A$ on $X$, namely $A\subset X\times X$, and a map $\Phi:X\to X$, we set 
    $$
    \Phi_*A = \{(\Phi(x),\Phi(y))\,|\,(x,y)\in A\}.
    $$ 
    %the binary relation of all pairs $(\Phi(x))$
    Given two binary flows $F_1,F_2$ on $X$ and a continuous map $\Phi$, we say that {\BF $\Phi$ preserves the prolongational relation} (resp., the Auslander relation) if $\Phi_*\NW_{F_1}=\NW_{F_2}$ (resp., $\Phi_*\cA_{F_1}=\cA_{F_2}$).
\end{definition}
