Notably, the index reveals a clear spatial pattern and identifies distinct clusters of fragility, specifically: 

\begin{itemize}
    \item The urban area of New York, Washington and Philadelphia seems to show the lowest levels of fragility, as well as the New England area and the Boston area. We can expect this result, as these are the most developed areas of the US. 
