%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%  abstract  %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

\begin{abstract}

We consider the existence of radially symmetric stationary solutions of the compressible viscous and heat-conductive polytropic ideal fluid on the unbounded exterior domain of a sphere in $\mathbb{R}^n (n\ge 3)$ where the boundary and far-field conditions are prescribed.
The unique existence of the stationary solution is shown for both inflow and outflow problems in a suitably small neighborhood of the far-field state.
Estimates of the algebraic decay rate toward the far field state are also obtained. 

%\aka{Furthermore, it is shown that 
%the boundary layer of the density appears as the velocity data tend to zero
%in the inflow problem, but not in the outflow problem. }


\end{abstract}

\medskip

