Therefore, we need a term structure that can not only perform well on one specific surface but also be robust against large variations owning to the surface dynamics. For this, we adapt the neural term structure as in Section~\ref{subsec:cali_seq} to train on a sequence of implied volatility surfaces to produce a set of term structures that have generally consistent shapes and also fit each specific surface.

