We end this subsection with the remark that our category of geometric stacks relative to the tuple \((\mathbf{Aff}_{\bD_{\geq 0}(K)}, \tau_{\bA}^{rat}, \mathbf{P}^{o-sm}, \bA_K)\) contains derived rigid analytic spaces (defined in \cite{soor2024derived}) as a full subcategory. Indeed, in loc.cit., Soor uses the same category of derived affinoids with the topology \(\tau^{rat}\) of derived rational localisations; he then defines his \(\infty\)-category \(\mathbf{dRig}_K\) of derived rigid spaces as the \(1\)-schemes with respect to the tuple \((\mathbf{Aff}_{\bD_{\geq 0}(K)}, \tau_{\bA}^{rat}, \mathbf{P}_\bA^{o-sm}, \bA_K)\). Summarily,

