 \end{corollary}


 \begin{proof}
  Let ${M_{i}:i\in\mathcal{I}}$ be a collection of $\pi$-torsion free $\pi$-adic $R$-modules. The product $\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}M_{i}$ consists of tuples $(m_{i})_{i\in\mathcal{I}}$ such that $\mathrm{sup}_{i\in\mathcal{I}}||m_{i}||_{i}<\infty$, with norm given by the supremum. Note that in fact the maximum will be achieved. Suppose that $||(m_{i})||=\delta^{l}$. Then $\forall i\in\mathcal{I}$, \(m_{i}=\delta^{l_{i}}n_{i}\) for some $l_{i}\ge l$ and some $n_{i}$ with $||n_{i}||=1$, and for some $i_{0}$, $l_{i_{0}}=l$. Thus $(m_{i})=\pi^{l}(\pi^{l_{i}-l}n_{i})$, and $\pi^{l_{i_{0}}-l}n_{i_{0}}=n_{i_{0}}$. Hence $(m_{i})\in\pi^{l}\prod_{i\in\mathcal{I}}M_{i}$.
