Let $R$ be an almost adic Banach ring with pseudo-uniformiser $\pi$. The \emph{affinoid Tate algebra in} $n$ variables is the free commutative monoid on $R^{\oplus n}$, computed in $\sf{Ban}_{R}^{\le1}$. We denote it by $R \gen{x_1, \dotsc, x_n}$, and we have 
 \[R \gen{x_1, \dotsc, x_n} \defeq \varprojlim_n R/(\pi^{k})[x_1, \dotsc, x_n],\] viewed as an algebra in \(\bD_{\geq 0}(\mathsf{Ban}_R^{\leq 1})^\circ \). 


