in which all maps are localisations. In particular, we have
$$\mathbf{Nuc}^{\infty}(U\cup V:V\cap Y)=\mathbf{QCoh}(U\cup V:(U\cup V)\cap Y)\cong\mathbf{Nuc}^{\infty}(V:Y\cap V)$$. 
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}
    The fibre product diagram comes from descent. The last claim follows from the fact that the horizontal maps have isomorphic fibres, since the diagram is a pullback.
