\begin{lemma}
Let $\mathbf{D}$ be equipped with a topology $\tau$.
    Let $\mathbf{E}=\mathbf{Cat}^{L}$ be the category of $(\infty,1)$-categories with maps being left adjoint functors, and let $\mathbf{Q}\in\mathbf{PreShv}(\mathbf{D};\mathbf{Cat}^{L})$ satisfy descent for $\tau$. Let $f:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}$ and $g:\mathcal{Y}\rightarrow\mathcal{Z}$ be maps in $\mathbf{Shv}(\mathbf{D})$ with $f$ being an effective epimorphism of stacks. Then $g\circ f$ satisfies $\mathbf{Q}$-descent if and only if $g$ satisfies $\mathbf{Q}$-descent.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
    Since $f:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}$ is an effective epimorphism in the topos of sheaves, we have 
    $$\overline{\mathrm{im}}(g\circ f)\cong\overline{\mathrm{im}}(g)$$
    for any $g$, where $\overline{\mathrm{im}}(h)$ denotes the image of $h$ in the topos of sheaves. Since $\mathbf{Q}$ satisfies descent for $\tau$ we have
    $$\mathbf{Q}(\overline{\mathrm{im}}(h))\cong\mathbf{Q}(\mathrm{im}(h))$$
    Thus to verify that a map of sheaves 
    $$h:\mathcal{V}\rightarrow\mathcal{W}$$ 
